* sg13g2-opamp -- large-signal step (slew-rate) bench, design/opamp_core.sch (issue #12)
* Generated from
* sim/slew-rate/testbench/tb_slew.spice.tmpl by
* sim/slew-rate/run_slew_sweep.sh -- do not edit a generated
* netlist-snapshots/*.spice file directly, edit this template and re-run
* the sweep.
*
* Point: corner=@@MOS_SECTION@@ temp_c=@@TEMP_C@@ vdd_v=@@VDD_V@@
* PDK: @@PDK@@ @@PDK_ROOT@@ (see sim/pdk.json for the pinned release)
* OSDI models: @@OSDI_DIR@@ (built by sim/tools/build-osdi.sh)
* DUT netlist snapshot: @@DUT_NETLIST@@ (frozen copy of
*   design/netlist/opamp_core.spice alongside this generated testbench, so
*   the exact DUT netlist this point ran against is reviewable later)
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------ method
* design/netlist/opamp_core.spice is a FLAT xschem netlist (its
* "**.subckt"/"**.ends" lines are full-line SPICE comments, not an active
* subcircuit wrapper), so .include'ing it makes its own node names (vdd,
* vss, inn, inp, out, ibias, plus the internal d1/d2/tail nodes) live
* directly at this testbench's top level -- same arrangement
* sim/open-loop-ac/testbench/tb_openloop_ac.spice.tmpl uses.
*
* DC bias: Lbreak = 1e18 H from inn to out, the same ideal-inductor DC
* feedback trick sim/open-loop-ac/ uses (an ideal inductor is a dead short
* at DC, so inn = out at DC and the loop self-consistently settles near a
* unity-gain-buffer bias point, Vout(dc) close to Vinp(dc) = Vcm = VDD/2),
* and an open circuit on this bench's nanosecond timescale (dI/dt = V/L,
* i.e. ~1e-18 A/s for a 1 V swing, so the inductor current -- and therefore
* the charge delivered to inn -- is frozen for the whole transient).
*
* Large-signal drive: the two inputs are stepped ANTIPHASE by @@VSTEP_V@@ V
* each, so the differential input is +/- 2*@@VSTEP_V@@ V while the input
* common mode stays fixed at Vcm = VDD/2. inp is driven directly; inn is
* driven through Cinj = 1 uF from the antiphase source node nstep, which is
* a short at these timescales (inn's own capacitance is M1's ~5 fF gate
* cap, so the coupling ratio is 1:1 to ~5 ppm) while leaving the Lbreak DC
* servo above to set inn's bias. run_slew_sweep.sh re-derives the achieved
* inn excursion per point from this file's own TR_VINN_* lines and fails
* the point if the drive did not arrive as intended.
*
* Why antiphase (and not a single-ended step into a unity-gain buffer):
* this amplifier's NMOS tail device has little Vds headroom at Vcm = VDD/2
* on the 1.08 V rail (design/opamp_sizing.md "Headroom check": tail node =
* Vcm - Vgs1, ~0.21 V nominal and less at the slow/cold corner). A
* single-ended step moves the input common mode by half the step, which
* moves the tail node, which moves the tail current -- and the tail current
* IS the quantity a slew measurement is trying to read. Measured during
* this bench's development at mos_ss/-40 C/1.08 V, a single-ended +/-0.15 V
* step produced 6.6 V/us rising against 2.5 V/us falling -- a 2.6x
* asymmetry that is a common-mode artifact of the drive, not a property of
* the amplifier; an antiphase drive of the SAME differential amplitude
* returns 5.30 / 5.15 V/us at that corner, and this bench's committed
* +/-0.3 V-per-input drive returns 7.54 / 7.51 V/us. See README.md "Why an
* antiphase differential drive" and "Choosing the drive amplitude".
*
* Step sequence (out is open-loop at these timescales, so each step drives
* the output all the way to a rail and the measured window sits in the
* linear ramp between them):
*   t = 0            inputs balanced at the DC bias point; out ~ Vcm
*   t = @@T1@@        step DOWN  -- out slews to the low rail and parks
*   t = @@T2@@        step UP    -- full-swing RISING edge  (measured)
*   t = @@T3@@        step DOWN  -- full-swing FALLING edge (measured)
*   t = @@T_STOP@@    end
*
* ibias: a single external ideal current-source bias pin, per
* design/opamp_sizing.md "Bias scope" -- 10 uA sunk from vdd through the
* ibias node into the DUT's own diode-connected Mbias. run_slew_sweep.sh
* reports total Vdd supply current AND this fixed 10 uA separately, per
* opamp_sizing.md's "Iq reporting note", exactly as sim/open-loop-ac/ does.
*
* Per-point DC sanity check (op landed near mid-rail, no internal node
* fully railed) is computed by run_slew_sweep.sh from this file's own
* echoed OP_* lines below -- same rule, and same honest scope, as
* sim/open-loop-ac/README.md "Per-point sanity checks" documents.

.lib "@@PDK_ROOT@@/@@PDK@@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerCAP.lib" cap_typ
.include "@@DUT_NETLIST@@"

.lib "@@PDK_ROOT@@/@@PDK@@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerMOSlv.lib" @@MOS_SECTION@@

.options temp=@@TEMP_C@@ tnom=27
* uniform output grid, so the committed waveform IS the data the recorded
* slew numbers are measured from (run_slew_sweep.sh re-reads this file's
* own wrdata output; nothing is computed from discarded internal steps)
.options interp

Vdd vdd 0 dc @@VDD_V@@
Vss vss 0 dc 0
Iibias vdd ibias dc 10u
Lbreak inn out 1e18
Cinj inn nstep 1e-6
Cload out vss @@CL_F@@
Vinp inp 0 dc @@VCM_V@@ pwl(0 @@VCM_V@@ @@T1@@ @@VCM_V@@ @@T1E@@ @@VP_LO@@ @@T2@@ @@VP_LO@@ @@T2E@@ @@VP_HI@@ @@T3@@ @@VP_HI@@ @@T3E@@ @@VP_LO@@ @@T_STOP@@ @@VP_LO@@)
Vstepn nstep 0 dc 0 pwl(0 0 @@T1@@ 0 @@T1E@@ @@VN_HI@@ @@T2@@ @@VN_HI@@ @@T2E@@ @@VN_LO@@ @@T3@@ @@VN_LO@@ @@T3E@@ @@VN_HI@@ @@T_STOP@@ @@VN_HI@@)

.control
pre_osdi @@OSDI_DIR@@/psp103.osdi
pre_osdi @@OSDI_DIR@@/psp103_nqs.osdi
pre_osdi @@OSDI_DIR@@/mosvar.osdi
pre_osdi @@OSDI_DIR@@/r3_cmc.osdi

op
echo "OP_VOUT $&v(out)"
echo "OP_VD1 $&v(d1)"
echo "OP_VD2 $&v(d2)"
echo "OP_VTAIL $&v(tail)"
echo "OP_VIBIAS $&v(ibias)"
let ivdd_op = -i(vdd)
echo "OP_IVDD $&ivdd_op"

tran @@T_PRINT@@ @@T_STOP@@ 0 @@T_MAX@@
let vinnmax = vecmax(v(inn))
let vinnmin = vecmin(v(inn))
let voutmax = vecmax(v(out))
let voutmin = vecmin(v(out))
echo "TR_VINN_MAX $&vinnmax"
echo "TR_VINN_MIN $&vinnmin"
echo "TR_VOUT_MAX $&voutmax"
echo "TR_VOUT_MIN $&voutmin"
wrdata @@TRAN_CSV@@ v(out)
.endc
.end
